{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfZfqU5BoNmy5dodJEPb3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written the candidate and it passes the self-check (`OK`). The smoke fit gave an ELPD-LOO of −1009.2. That is close to the incumbent's −1008.5, but a 100-draw, one-chain fit is too noisy to say which is better.\n\n**What I chose:** I refined `windowed_glimpse_expectation`, the live model tied with the incumbent at rank 1. In that model, people read a sequence through a short memory window and judge it random when the heads/tails mix of each glimpse looks like what they'd expect from a random coin.\n\n**The one change:** each person now has their own memory-window width, where before everyone shared one. It is drawn from a population distribution, set up the same way as the existing personal switch-rate belief. People with a narrow window judge mostly by how often the flips alternate. People with a wide window notice overall heads/tails balance and long runs. This is aimed at the critique's strongest finding, the one that survives the false-discovery correction: people differ more in how much they prefer the more balanced sequence than the incumbent's single shared balance weight allows (observed spread 0.18 vs 0.143 predicted, q = 0.016).\n\n**Name:** `personal_span_glimpse_expectation`\n\n**Files:**\n- `.../iter_2/candidate_5/hypothesis.md`\n- `.../iter_2/candidate_5/model_name.txt`\n- `.../iter_2/candidate_5/candidate.py`, which is the original model's source with only the memory-window parameter and its docstring changed.\n\n**Risks at admission:**\n- **Unreliable LOO estimate:** 7.5% of trials had Pareto k above 0.5, against a 1% tolerance. A longer production fit may bring that down; if not, the model's ELPD-LOO can't be trusted, and it couldn't be chosen as the winner even if admitted.\n- **Convergence untested:** a one-chain fit can't report R-hat, so the check doesn't cover it. Admission requires R-hat ≤ 1.05, bulk ESS ≥ 100 and almost no divergent transitions.\n- **Novelty untested:** the check doesn't compare predictions against the model I refined. Admission rejects the candidate if its predictions stay too close to that model's across the stimulus space."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2139,"cache_read_input_tokens":58531,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2139,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0e0f2c0a-eb1e-4db5-8021-9f7048264277","uuid":"9b245b6b-f7c5-44f8-8cdc-2e6d2ef213e8","timestamp":"2026-09-30T13:03:54.806Z","request_id":"req_011CfZfqSXQqeg8MzzryMpUH"}
